From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:41:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SIDsound::doEnvelopeGenerator: keep the envelope level to 8
 bits

An attack starting at level 0xFF (a gate turned off and on again while
sustaining at full level) counted on to 0x1FF before switching to decay,
which then read envGenDRdivisors[0x1FF], past the table. The level now
wraps from 0xFF to 0, as in reSID, and comes back to 0xFF.
---
 src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp b/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp
index a53f70f..e93b86b 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp
@@ -509,7 +509,11 @@ inline int SIDsound::doEnvelopeGenerator(unsigned int cycles, SIDVoice &v)
 
 				case EG_ATTACK:
 					// According to Bob Yannes, Attack is linear...
-					if ( ((++v.envCurrLevel) & 0xFF) == 0xFF) {
+					// An 8-bit counter: from 0xFF it wraps to 0, as in reSID.
+					// It counted on to 0x1FF, and decay then read past
+					// envGenDRdivisors.
+					v.envCurrLevel = (v.envCurrLevel + 1) & 0xFF;
+					if (v.envCurrLevel == 0xFF) {
 						v.egState = EG_DECAY;
 						v.envCounterCompare = v.envDecaySub;
 					}
